    "field": "Climate modeling",
    "problem": "Existing climate modeling inadequately assesses forecast uncertainty because computational limitations prevent running the massive number of simulations required to systematically explore the full range of uncertain model parameters, thereby hindering robust probabilistic predictions and public engagement.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a distributed computing method where volunteers run a massive ensemble of climate model simulations with perturbed parameters on their home PCs to generate a probabilistic forecast that better quantifies uncertainty.",
    "task": "The task is to generate a probabilistic climate forecast by using a distributed computing network of volunteers' home PCs to run a massive ensemble of climate model simulations, thereby better exploring the uncertainty in predictions.",
