            "target_entity_instance": "coupled",
            "target_entity_type": "SimulationType",
            "paragraph": "Hundreds of thousands of 50-year integrations would be required to explore all the relevant parameter combinations in a full-scale climate model. This is well beyond the capacity of current and planned modelling facilities. Or is it? The 'HadCM3' model from the UK Meteorological Office is one of the latest generation of coupled models used in the IPCC2000 Third Assessment Report. A single 50-year integration would take about six months on a reasonably up-to-date home personal computer, while the memory and disk-storage requirements are no larger than those of an advanced computer game.",
